Evident creator

        (1) by a truth of practical reason, absent knowledge of whether there exists
          a ground (stable ground) and, if so, what it consists in, that knowledge
          (ground knowledge) is itself a ground (the default ground)
            : re `^*\(\d+\) (.+)`s see `^*argue\+ that, ${same}`p @ default/._/text.notes.brec
        (2) despite long efforts [in the past], ultimately|{in the end} {we have}|{∃ among us}
          (at present) no settled consensus on the ground question [or its likes]
            : re `the ground question` viz. `whether there exists a ground.+and.+what it consists in`p
        (3) we know|have (at present) of no way|method to [reliably]
          {gauge|determine|predict an upper limit|bound on}|bound
          {how long}|{the period|{length of time}} it could|might take to acquire ground knowledge
          or deal with any stable ground we thereby apprehend

        : see `^*\(1\)`
        : see `^*\(2\)`
        : see `^*\(3\)` : ∴ (4)
       ────────────────
        (4) practical reason directs us to carry on for a period of time that in prospect
          (given our present state of knowledge) would be open-ended and likely long
        (5) a safehold highly fit to secure the long-term survival of mind-bearing populations
          extends throughout the cosmos
            : ad `long-term` : over periods on the scale of cosmogonal time,
              as opposed to the (relatively short) scale of geogenic time
                : re `scale of cosmogonal time`
                  see `stability on the longer ${same}` @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
                : re `\(relatively short\) scale of geogenic time`
                  see `the scope.+not restricted to.+the ${same}`s @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
            : re `(a safehold.+to secure the.+survival of) (mind)-bearing (populations)`p
              see `${1} ${3} of beings \(like us\) that have ${2}`p @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec

        : see `^*\(4\)`
        : see `^*\(5\)` : ∴ (6)
       ────────────────
        (6) the safehold’s fitness as a means coincides with the end to which reason
          (in our present state) directs us

    - the coincidence surprises because it lacks for an obvious explanation
    - an obvious place to begin looking, however, is the aetiology of the safehold
    - an aetiologic survey that aims for exhaustive coverage by typological division
      turns up the following results


            table, Known, possible explanantia for the safehold
                ┈

              explain-  truth mode    name of explanans
               able    of explanans

                yes
                        necessary
                                      physical necessity

                                      supernatural design

                    ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈
                        contingent
                                      natural cosmogonal selection

                                      constrained multiverse ensemble

                                      mundane design

                ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈
                no
                                      null, brute fact


        : re `an aetiologic survey.+by typological division`
          see `^*Allan.+2026.+Aetiology of the cosmic safehold` @ sources.brec

    - none of these in itself can explain the coincidence
        - each known explanans for the safehold is either null or given to be indeterminate
            : re `given.+indeterminate` see `^*• .+explainable by a \(yet unknown\) theory` @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : re `given.+indeterminate` see `^*• God had reason \(yet unknown\) to make the safehold` @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : re `given.+indeterminate` see `^*• .+cull of a \(yet unknown\) natural process` @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : re `given.+indeterminate` see `^*• .+bound.+by a \(yet unknown\) constraint`s @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : re `given.+indeterminate` see `^*• cosmocrafters have reason \(yet unknown\) to.+craft`s @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
        - therefore none quite suffices to explain even the safehold,
          let alone the coincidence in which it takes part
    - yet reason also takes part, and some of the explanatia can be determined by the part that it takes
        - these are the artificial, design explanantia
        - there are two of them

            • supernatural design by God
                : re `^*• (.+ design) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            • mundane design by cosmic creators
                : re `^*• (.+ design) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec

        (7) the mind of a creative designer (as figures in the two design explanantia) can both
          conform to practical-rational ground direction and (within range of its competence)
          mediate the causation of things (artifacts) as effects of that conformance
        (8) competent cosmic designers/creators are given in both design explanantia

        : see `^*\(7\)`
        : see `^*\(8\)` : ∴ (9)
       ────────────────
        (9) the creatable artifacts of (7) would (in the case of a design explanans)
          include artifacts of cosmic structure such as the safehold

        : see `^*\(7\)`
        : see `^*\(9\)` : ∴ (10)
       ────────────────
        (10) the explanans of supernatural design might be determined by a stable ground unknown to us
          (at present), but known to God, that entails our long-term persistence


        : see `^*\(1\)`
        : see `^*\(7\)`
        : see `^*\(9\)` : ∴ (11)
       ────────────────
        (11) the explanans of mundane design might be determined by the default ground

        : see `^*\(10\)`
        : see `^*\(11\)` : ∴ (12)
       ────────────────
        (12) it is clear how each design explanans might be determined such that it explains
          both the safehold and the coincidence in which it takes part

    - the same does not apply to the other non-null explanantia
        - these are the natural explanantia
        - there are three of them

            • physical necessity entailing a safehold
                : re `• (physical necessity) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            • cosmogonal path selection tending toward safeholding
                : re `• (.+) path (s.+?) .+` see `^^na.+${1} ${2}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            • multiverse ensemble constrained toward safeholding
                : re `• (.+) (constrained) .+` see `^^${2} ${1}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec

        (13) it is unclear how any of the natural explanantia might be determined to include a mechanism
          or process, aside from mind as it figures in the design explanantia, that does the same work
            : ad `the same work` : explains both the safehold and the coincidence in which it takes part
                : re `: (explains.+)`s see `^*\(12\).+${same}`sp

        : see `^*\(12\)`
        : see `^*\(13\)` : ∴ (14)
       ────────────────
        (14) the two design explanantia have the greatest explanatory power
          among all known, possible explanantia for the safehold

        : see `^*\(14\)` : ∴ (15)
       ────────────────
        (15) belief in the disjunction of the two design explanantia would be justified
            : ad `the disjunction of the two design explanantia` : supernatural ∨ mundane
